      en: "The largest limestone cave system in East Africa, historically used as a refuge and for traditional ceremonies. Formed during the Jurassic period. Significant place of worship for locals. Numerous stalactites and stalagmites. Many unexplored passages. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Tanzania — an East African country shaped by Mount Kilimanjaro, the Serengeti, the Ngorongoro Crater, Lake Victoria and Lake Tanganyika, the Zanzibar archipelago along the Indian Ocean coast, and its wealth in coffee, cloves and gold mining — and offers insight into the regional identity."
